# Files that must never reach a deployment.
#
# Python functions have no tree-shaking: they bundle everything reachable at build time. A
# `functions.excludeFiles` glob does not help for a framework service, because the whole service
# builds as a single function rather than one per source file - so the glob matches nothing and
# fails silently. This file is the control that actually applies.
#
# Verified by inspecting the built bundle's filePathMap, not by assuming.

# Private working memory. Gitignored, and must not leave the machine.
.agent/

# Tests, generators, and evaluation data: build-time and research artifacts, never served.
tests/
tools/
eval/
docs/
.github/

# Large local caches and downloads.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash. A bare `data/` matches at ANY depth, which also excluded
# `backend/science/data/` -- the bundled star, moon, asteroid and atmosphere datasets. The four
# routes that read them returned 500 in production while every other route worked, because the
# service imported fine and only failed when a request reached the missing file.
/data/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/

# Secrets, in case one is ever present locally.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
